                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16608951" author="zjffdu" created="Mon, 10 Sep 2018 10:00:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=aweise&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;aweise&quot;&gt;aweise&lt;/a&gt; The latest zeppelin will show binded interpreter dynamically, that means if you have one paragraph starting with %spark, then spark interpreter will show in the interpreter binding memu. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16610152" author="aweise" created="Tue, 11 Sep 2018 06:25:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;What for multiple spark interpreter scenario, e.g.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;%spark_foo&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;%spark_bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Endusers are used to say only %pyspark in paragraph and set the desired default interpreter in the binding menu accordingly.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That way, they can switch between interpreters (e.g. with different sizings) easily. They don&apos;t have to change every paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16784259" author="aweise" created="Tue, 5 Mar 2019 09:41:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=moon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;moon&quot;&gt;moon&lt;/a&gt; Can we add this as blocker for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4022&quot; title=&quot;Release 0.9.0&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-4022&quot;&gt;ZEPPELIN-4022&lt;/a&gt;. It&apos;s the actual Bug for the bahavior change that has been introduced with &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3594&quot; title=&quot;Remove interpreter binding&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-3594&quot;&gt;ZEPPELIN-3594&lt;/a&gt;. Also see my comment &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3594?focusedCommentId=16598289&amp;amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-16598289&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16785145" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 6 Mar 2019 01:39:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=aweise&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;aweise&quot;&gt;aweise&lt;/a&gt; I have linked that&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17035004" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 12 Feb 2020 02:48:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=aweise&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;aweise&quot;&gt;aweise&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pbrenner&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pbrenner&quot;&gt;pbrenner&lt;/a&gt;&#160;I have created PR for it, could you help try and review it ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17036759" author="zjffdu" created="Fri, 14 Feb 2020 07:49:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 3641&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3641&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3641&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17074040" author="pbrenner" created="Thu, 2 Apr 2020 19:32:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt;&#160;has this broken again? I have notebooks that show no interpreters even after I start a paragraph with %spark_foo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Note that we just installed 0.9 today and for whatever reason lost all of our interpreters so we are recreating them from scratch.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;paragraphs run fine with the new interpreters if I start with %spark_foo in each one but that is going to be not possible to add to every paragraph in hundreds of notebooks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is possible this is a different issue (if so, I can create a new ticket). When I click the gear icon to pick interpreters it shows nothing and immediately pops up &quot;Interpreter setting changes will be discarded.&quot; So perhaps it is specific to notebooks that were set to use a particular interpreter that no longer exists? Let me know if there should be a new ticket.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
